{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q012_not_true_family_specific_pair","answer":"Yes, within SCOPe 2.08 they are classified as homologous. Both domains sit in the same family, k.40.1.1 "Designed trimeric coiled-coil" (family sunid 100905). Both are also in the same superfamily (k.40.1, sunid 100904), fold (k.40, sunid 100903) and class (k, Designed proteins, sunid 58788). The two domains differ only at the protein level. d1s9za_ (1s9z A:, domain sunid 98768) is in protein "Amyloidogenic design-1" (sunid 103785). d1hqja_ (1hqj A:, domain sunid 61142) is in protein "Unnamed design-1" (sunid 100906). Both have species "Synthetic".

The annotation and homology responses for both domains show no inconsistencies, repeats, heterogeneity or warnings, and no nf (not-a-true-fold) or similar flag. The only comments are ligand notes: d1s9za_ is complexed with na and zn, and d1hqja_ with pb, sin and so4. So no returned caveat undermines the same-family placement.

The limits matter. The class is "Designed proteins", so the shared family reflects a shared engineered coiled-coil design and fold. It is not evidence of natural evolutionary descent. Here "homologous" means only that SCOPe's family and superfamily levels assert it. Different protein names do not mean different families, and I did not check sequence identity. The placement does not show that the two designs have the same function, amyloidogenic behavior, oligomeric state, ligand binding or interchangeable template use. The ligand comments are crystallization context, not functional evidence. This conclusion applies to release 2.08 only. I did not query other releases, so I make no claim about historical reclassification.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","mcp__scope__compare_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1s9za_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1hqja_/homology"]}]}
